<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $25.14 bln on March 21.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $25.14 bln on March 21.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $25.14 billion on March 21, 1997 from $24.66 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Mar 21	Mar 14	 Mar 22</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     21,160	20,680	 16,803</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,977	 3,977	  4,659</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	     2		9</p>
<p>    Total			     25,139	24,659	 21,471</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
